<span class="cat-badge">Guide &middot; Monthly Rental</span>
<h1>Teachers: Parking and Security Planning in Hanoi | Hanoi Motorbike Guide</h1>
<p>A teacher&rsquo;s motorbike in Hanoi spends its week in two great parked stretches, the long patient day inside or beside the school and the night at the home base, with short hops between, and the security of the whole arrangement is really the security of those two places plus the small habits that carry everything else. A month of daily riding makes parking the term&rsquo;s most repeated decision, made twice a day at minimum, and decisions repeated that often deserve planning rather than improvisation. This page plans them honestly, school gate, home base and street layer, without inventing a parking rule, price or policy that only each school, each street and each counter can state.</p>
<p>The machine underneath the plan comes from Motorbike Rental - Nguyen Tu at 112 Nguyen Van Cu in Long Bien, open daily 09:00 to 21:00, and the security conversation starts at the handover. Start at the <a href="/monthly-motorbike-rental-hanoi/">monthly motorbike rental in Hanoi</a> hub, weigh the rates at the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental-cost/">Hanoi motorbike rental cost</a> guide, see the fleet and terms at the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental/">Hanoi motorbike rental</a> page, read the <a href="/monthly-motorbike-rental-hanoi/motorbike-rental-for-expats-hanoi/">motorbike rental for expats</a> guide for the long-stay picture, and browse the <a href="/motorbike-guides/">motorbike guides</a> for the street habits that keep a working month quiet.</p>
<nav class="toc">
<ol>
<li><a href="#sec-1">The term&rsquo;s two parked places</a></li>
